meta {
  name: Upload Branding Logo
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/branding/logo
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(logo.png)
  alt: Gemeente Voorbeeld
}

docs {
  Stores a new logo. platform_admin only. Point the file part at a local PNG.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Body capped at 1 MB (413 payload_too_large).
    2. file: PNG signature sniffed (declared type and name ignored), at most
       512 KB, 16x16 to 2000x800 pixels (read from the header before the
       image is decoded), fully decoded so a corrupt body is refused.
    3. alt: 1 to 255 characters; whitespace folded.
    4. Nothing is stored on rejection.
    5. Writes branding.logo_updated to audit_logs with before/after
       { width, height, alt, size_bytes, sha256 } (never the bytes).

  Enabling a custom logo on a public production instance needs Rijkshuisstijl
  sign-off.

  Responses:
    200 OK — same body as GET /api/v1/branding
    401 unauthorized / 403 forbidden — not platform_admin
    413 payload_too_large
    422 validation_failed — file: required | too_large | unsupported_type |
        invalid_image | invalid_dimensions; alt: invalid
}
